Engraving with a spell should take the same time as engraving with your 
fingers.

Cancellation, cone of cold, create monster, dig, detect unseen, finger 
of death, force bolt, knock, light, magic missile, polymorph, sleep, 
slow monster, teleport away, turn undead, and wizard lock should simply 
duplicate the effect of the equivalent wand.

Fireball: duplicate the effect of a wand of fire.
Haste self: duplicate the effect of a wand of speed monster.
Invisibility: duplicate the effect of a wand of invisibility.

Clairvoyance, create familiar, cure blindness, cure sickness, detect 
food, detect monsters, detect treasure, identify, magic mapping, 
protection, remove curse, and restore ability should simply have the 
usual effects of the spell when used to engrave.

Cause fear: "The bugs on the floor huddle in fright."
Charm monster: "The bugs on the floor start following you."
Confuse monster: "The bugs on the floor look confused."
Drain life: "The bugs on the floor look weaker."
Extra healing: "The bugs on the floor look much better."
Healing: "The bugs on the floor look better."
Jumping: cause the engraving to appear randomly in jumping distance.
Levitation: "The words drift off the ground" and the engraving vanishes.
Stone to flesh: "The edges on the floor get smoother" and the engraving 
is corrupted.

The great thing is, none of these would break bones compatibility. 
